{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" initial=\"p\">\n  <state id=\"p\" initial=\"a\">\n    <state id=\"a\">\n      <transition target=\"p\"/>\n    </state>\n  </state>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint008-default-entry-loop.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":0,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":1},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint008-default-entry-loop.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":28,"endLine":4,"startColumn":27,"startLine":4}}}],"message":{"markdown":"eventless transitions loop forever without consuming an event: `a` -> `a`\n\n**Note:** each step is the first eventless transition without `cond` on the active state's ancestor chain, so it is always selected; default entry through `initial` targets closes the loop\n\n**Help:** add an `event` or `cond` to one of these transitions, or retarget one so the macrostep can reach a stable configuration\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.13 Selecting and Executing Transitions","text":"eventless transitions loop forever without consuming an event: `a` -> `a`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":149,"start":148},"category":"lint"},"ruleId":"LINT008"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"each step is the first eventless transition without `cond` on the active state's ancestor chain, and default entry through `initial` leads back to the start, so the interpreter never reaches a stable configuration (a warning: SCXML 1.0 Appendix D says a macrostep that does not terminate \"is currently allowed\", so the document is conforming and compiles, and a host bounds the run)"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: add an `event` or `cond` to one transition in the loop, or retarget one so the macrostep can settle.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §3.13 Selecting and Executing Transitions\n\nRun `scx --explain LINT008` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#SelectingTransitions","id":"LINT008","name":"LINT008","properties":{"category":"lint"},"shortDescription":{"text":"eventless transitions loop forever through default entry"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}